  "profile": "mooring.batch-resolution.v0.4",
  "status": "shared-planner-regression-vectors-not-transport-conformance",
  "rules": [
    "Known immutable outcomes are not revalidated. Definite admission failures and their transitive dependents are excluded from outgoing SCC edges.",
    "Detect complete operation and atomic-change SCCs among remaining eligible changes; cycles precede acyclic internal forward-order errors.",
    "Preserve operation order. Whole-change application follows stable topological order.",
    "Adapter failure names an actual immutable member. It alone receives the direct reason; atomic siblings and descendants retain its original root.",
    "Group admission failure roots deterministically at the first member unless the validator identifies an actual failing member.",
    "This shared intersection does not cover identity-conflict persistence, transport/schema validation, authorization or engine correctness."
